<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermen Rode</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1430–<a href="/years/1504">1504</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermen Rode was a painter based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, one of the leading artists of the Hanseatic world in the late 15th century. His surviving works include the high altar of St Nicholas' Church in Tallinn (Reval), completed in 1481, and the St Luke altarpiece in Lübeck, showing the strong artistic links between Lübeck and the Baltic towns.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Lübeck artist Bernt Notke painted the Danse Macabre now displayed in St Nicholas' Church and the altarpiece of the Church of the Holy Spirit, while <b>Hermen Rode</b>'s high altar survives in St Nicholas.</blockquote><a href="/empire/reval">Reval · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=53.87,10.69&amp;year=1478" aria-label="Lübeck on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4787 314 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Hermen Rode"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5237 584h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5237 584h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=53.87,10.69&amp;year=1478">What was here in 1478? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
